11	2	1	1	<markdown>\n\nI think you might be a regulatory consultant because the question is about law, regulation, or policy.\n\nHere I provide the answer to your question regarding the specific requirements for cosmetic product facility registration and product listing under the Modernization of Cosmetics Regulation Act of 2022:\n\nThe FDA requires that by December 29, 2023, cosmetic product facilities must be registered, and products must be listed according to section 607 of the FD&C Act. However, enforcement of these requirements is delayed until July 1, 2024, to give the industry additional time to comply. The registration and listing process involves submitting various pieces of information, including facility registration numbers, product details, and responsible person contact information. \n\n### References\n\n- Guidance - Cosmetics - Registration Listing-12-02-24\n\n  - > "Under section 607(c)(4)(B) of the FD&C Act, a single listing submission for a cosmetic product may include multiple cosmetic products with identical formulations, or formulations that differ only with respect to colors, fragrances or flavors, or quantity of contents."\n\n    This context explains that multiple products with similar formulations can be included in a single listing submission, simplifying the process for entities with such products.\n\n  - > "Under section 607(c) of the FD&C Act, the following information must be submitted in a cosmetic product listing: the facility registration number of each facility where the cosmetic product is manufactured or processed; the name and contact number of the responsible person and the name for the cosmetic product, as such name appears on the label; the applicable cosmetic category or categories for the cosmetic product..."\n\n    This is relevant as it details the specific information required for cosmetic product listing, which is crucial for compliance.\n\n- Guidance-CompliancePolicyCosmeticRegistrationListing-11032023\n\n  - > "FDA will be ready to accept registration and listing information by the statutory deadline of December 29, 2023, and we encourage companies to meet that deadline if they are able to do so. However, FDA does not intend to enforce the requirements under section 607 of the FD&C Act related to cosmetic product facility registration and cosmetic product listing for an additional six months after the December 29, 2023, statutory deadline, or until July 1, 2024..."\n\n    This context explains the timeline for enforcement of the registration and listing requirements, which is crucial for planning compliance activities.\n\n</markdown>	text	2025-02-23 21:54:58.495947-08	bot	Generate
