isting to avoid non-compliance.\n\n  - > "FDA also requests that the following additional optional information be submitted: product webpage link; whether the cosmetic product is for professional use only; Unique Ingredient Identifiers (UNIIs); and type of business (as listed on the label), i.e., manufacturer, packer, or distributor; image of the label (currently jpg files are accepted)."\n\n    This context emphasizes the need for accurate labeling and disclosure of product information as part of compliance efforts.\n\n  - > "The responsible person will need to obtain the relevant facility registration number(s) for each facility where its cosmetic products are manufactured or processed, because the facility registration number(s) is required for the product listing submission."\n\n    This context underscores the requirement for providing facility information to ensure compliance with FDA regulations.\n\n</markdown>	text	2025-02-23 22:00:02.938324-08	bot	Generate
