159	1	**ii.**<br><br>**Should FDA collect a 702(b) portion if documentation of interstate**\n**commerce is not immediately available?**<br><br>An FDA investigator must collect a 702(b) portion for an official sample, unless an exception \napplies. (See 21 CFR 2.10(a)(1) and section A.2. of this guidance for the meaning of official \nsample, which includes, among other things, evidence of interstate commerce.) <br><br>In some situations, such as a retail setting or as part of FDA’s surveillance activities, records or \nevidence of interstate commerce may not be immediately available at the time of the sample \ncollection. However, if FDA has reason to believe that the product was introduced into or in \ninterstate commerce and expects to obtain evidence of interstate commerce at a later time, FDA \nshould collect a 702(b) portion for the sample.	[0,845)	[-0.2688902,-0.69057226,0.7134596,0.14275035,-0.42924103,-0.51892513,0.21080624,-1.0853976,0.27711353,0.7734487,-0.260545,-0.5013993,-0.41623172,0.2830204,-0.41717723,0.9561875,0.008956562,-0.064615056,0.10569742,-0.24723737,-0.2425323,-0.46814463,-0.65110725,0.4854357,0.18327099,0.65709364,0.018320346,0.9363485,0.6232284,0.36740786,0.16658302,0.25540492,-0.16972344,-0.31739432,-0.14222135,-0.8924661,-0.9327665,0.35339358,0.31312513,0.38284403,-0.54001635,0.60975504,-0.38841075,0.37051356,-0.5256008,0.1713539,-0.19322008,-0.30873698,-0.3634258,-0.017720712,-0.26409674,-0.7969325,0.5276899,-0.618651,0.5903967,0.5498022,1.5078475,-0.29755932,-0.85630476,-0.11892005,-0.53148925,0.66279244,-0.68447155,0.015534071,0.52341187,0.45514783,-0.14648785,-0.972451,-0.6725176,-0.111779146,-0.16096266,-0.024621064,-0.048944235,-0.15269062,0.32518134,0.74470365,0.030317498,-0.31235632,-0.94892967,-0.057332184,0.6729843,0.09553356,0.3608182,0.045500815,-0.67819244,0.08245792,-1.0306922,0.40025237,0.35472605,0.34479073,-0.34430575,0.21423952,-0.22749706,0.3754137,0.72301716,0.07265894,0.27601784,-0.54763,-0.38524073,0.33673343,0.59155