317	1	Act and 21 CFR 207.1 and 807.3. \n13 By virtue of applying to both drug and device establishments, section 704(a)(4) of the FD&C Act also applies to \nestablishments that manufacture, prepare, propagate, compound, or process combination products (see section \n503(g)(1)(C) of the FD&C Act) and the drug and device constituent part(s) (defined under 21 CFR Part 4) of such \ncombination products. Establishments that engage in the manufacture, preparation, propagation, compounding, or \nprocessing of combination products that are not subject to the authorities under section 704(a)(4) of the FD&C Act \nmay voluntarily participate in an RRA. \n14 FDA intends to clearly indicate when we consider an activity to be an RRA so establishments can differentiate \nRRA interactions from non-RRA interactions. \n15 FD&C Act, section 704(a)(1). Relatedly, for requests for records and other information under section 704(a)(4), \nFDA does not intend to issue a Form FDA 482, Notice of Inspection or Form FDA 483, Inspectional Observations \nduring the RRA process.	[249,1296)	[-0.052133076,-0.8179086,0.509181,0.47595024,-0.055922214,-0.31073543,0.27811036,-0.7844593,0.5351056,0.8214112,-0.29210687,-0.44663683,-0.38604036,0.3391984,0.054507684,1.0096916,-0.40677708,0.081196316,-0.13217437,-0.4157507,-0.9828336,-0.68505585,-0.5782361,0.04936454,0.99100816,0.19611359,0.07203063,0.08608921,0.66273296,0.5191604,0.43928427,0.082456425,-0.006903927,-0.10619912,-0.1504271,-0.6312108,-1.0133775,0.20062628,0.36948952,0.49223956,-0.3684587,0.004112527,-0.4121089,0.97087353,-0.6852764,0.021433273,0.018624386,-0.08670967,-0.10783374,-0.4511133,-0.30862325,-0.69449776,0.108917065,-0.35599598,0.48181364,0.23760663,0.66175383,-0.15164942,-0.39077014,-0.43083292,-0.6621983,0.49695784,-0.57855856,0.5383616,0.16349019,0.005187411,-0.7409332,-0.78950393,-0.61989915,-0.35479093,-0.47017238,-0.28976136,-0.032519788,0.25176755,0.35978973,0.82820106,-0.6812811,-0.5991178,-0.9515822,0.3535782,0.42534116,0.0