356	1	><br>discuss such observations in sufficient detail to enable understanding and foster an appropriate response. \nFor purposes of this guidance, RRA observations are defined as conditions and/or practices observed \nduring the RRA that indicate, in the judgment of the FDA employee(s) conducting the RRA, a potential \nviolation of the laws enforced by FDA. FDA does not intend to issue a Form FDA 483, Inspectional <br><br>confirmed during an inspection and included on a Form 483). <br><br>439 An establishment should be aware that a written list of observations may be subject to a request under the \n440 \n441 \n442 \n443  Freedom of Information Act at the time the disclosure to the establishment is first made (see 21 CFR \n20.101(a)) and may be made publicly available, with applicable redaction of information that is exempt \nfrom public disclosure (see, e.g., 5 U.S.C. 552(b), 18 U.S.C. 1905, 21 U.S.C. 331(j), 360j(c), 360nn(e), \nand 387f(c), and 21 C.F.R. Part 20).	[464,1433)	[0.0015627719,-0.44254598,0.55583483,0.3898857,-0.1421422,-1.0637624,0.21000813,-1.1154897,0.511512,1.1950495,-0.53689307,-0.64774734,-0.60250586,0.6999863,-0.30278894,1.3885146,-0.122022785,-0.30489612,0.037577897,-0.15617827,-0.6609743,-0.30097064,-0.020423904,0.35318455,0.7272678,0.5822205,0.14261533,0.74565595,0.98933744,0.36494976,0.43147036,0.30646238,-0.38379973,-0.26382163,-0.11263582,-0.7287943,-0.7341418,0.22131623,0.6344707,0.25018597,-0.482284,0.27911454,-0.45039502,1.1082864,-0.68956983,0.16611657,-0.00094331766,0.026924394,-0.10327413,-0.31569782,-0.35720927,-0.9053317,0.45282832,-0.5623791,0.36148456,0.27928823,1.1027213,0.07833987,-0.3326513,-0.4066652,-0.634029,0.41474617,-0.8559764,0.6346022,0.75306183,-0.026742551,-0.079406716,-0.7646483,-0.5781489,-0.10600742,-0.6211829,-0.08399034,-0.45556477,-0.017012328,0.63072217,0.55375195,-0.48971966,-0.6938767,-0.8032673,0.3936823,0.60396093,-0.08405787,0.01526268,0.07058673,-0.7334239,-0.30404562,-0.5768692,-0.14186154,0.210557