461	1	The International Cooperation on Cosmetics Regulation and regions such as Canada and the \nEuropean Union have set a limit of 10 ppm for lead as an impurity in cosmetics based on \nconsiderations of a reasonably achievable level, scientific risk assessment, good manufacturing \npractices, technical feasibility, and appropriate analytical methods (Refs. 1, 2). This guidance is \nconsistent with those efforts.	[0,407)	[0.4885376,-0.6028044,0.43231243,0.47352755,0.10769656,-0.0018370454,-0.00415832,0.08693267,-0.15504724,0.35726106,-0.7229919,-1.0299565,-0.30105835,0.21696061,0.19513316,0.6024052,0.04583809,0.5883084,-0.024974985,0.36146802,-0.8876225,-0.10894449,-0.37618732,0.51958305,-0.036634136,1.3024235,0.585752,-0.03297884,0.8721929,0.08294056,-0.51265824,0.15755777,-0.5137075,0.1435391,-0.53864413,-0.6203831,-1.0770303,0.84148896,0.0269525,0.75543183,-0.2821575,0.05023303,-0.025850022,0.8083346,-0.47669578,-0.041054703,-0.0932236,-0.29331282,-0.3458266,0.23532528,-0.73338145,-0.22178009,0.328666,-0.75811315,0.45624304,0.3150763,1.0816677,-0.010669404,-0.2618548,-0.12878758,-0.07895971,1.2787439,-0.7697717,-0.13675036,0.43920156,0.02950478,-0.25430527,-0.5816341,-0.49276558,-0.1394888,-0.2713456,0.6576285,0.15868902,-0.5897911,0.27397168,0.57281274,-0.29643574,-0.15802188,-0.6163333,0.033970136,0.9858021,-0.034824036,0.66170424,0.003355254,-0.4804888,0.46745256,-1.6517652,-0.18484038,-0.095602855,0.6992072,-0.39388147,0.7602,-0.13791041,0.38054565,0.624034,0.7325328,0.14378594,-1.2239919,-0.26459664,-0.07839672,0.2802985,0.89617604,0.37369296,0.40473348,0.663829,-0.064338066,0.15932645,-1.2735182,-0.6016012,0.07578148,-0.6915609,-0.07664851,0.5737921,-0.7660755,-0.34231743,0.21434176,-0.09004313,-0.13573834,-0.09646508,-0.014409602,0.021615937,0.4394781,0.4300149,-0.8901544,0.64541054,0.1445096,0.7391998,-0.48251882,0.30804777,-0.37623304,-0.06837289,-0.65968525,0.51046664,-0.026860902,-0.55289924,-0.5940773,0.8381541,0.093220785,-1.0310849,0.44652447,-0.30