644	1	**I. INTRODUCTION**<br><br>This document provides guidance to industry sponsors, applicants, and petitioners \n(referred to collectively as*sponsors*) who develop, prepare, or submit briefing materials \nthat will be given to advisory committee members as background information before an \nopen FDA advisory committee meeting.2 This guidance will help sponsors develop, \norganize, and submit advisory committee briefing materials for public release and should \nhelp minimize the time and resources spent in preparing these materials for public \navailability. The guidance also describes the process FDA intends to follow when we \nmake briefing materials available to the public. In addition, the Appendices provide \nrecommended timelines for preparing and submitting briefing materials to us.3 <br><br>An important goal of this guidance is to help ensure that briefing materials are made \navailable to the public as provided under section 10(b) of the Federal Advisory \nCommittee Act (FACA) (5 U.S.C. App. 2). The guidance includes recommendations on	[0,1048)	[-0.2777489,-0.19584005,0.71829957,0.85722435,-0.35505462,-0.2935519,0.13449056,-0.8106975,0.32347113,0.9023938,-0.3365011,-0.5301642,-0.54236245,0.30867195,-0.14426373,1.0806488,-0.18951114,-0.27536935,-0.27183333,0.16866021,-0.3570279,-0.28010726,-0.105887175,0.460523,0.824257,0.448166,0.21925297,1.1482795,0.5962874,0.271684,-0.29614323,-0.11254641,-0.28779534,-0.27025938,-0.1040605,-0.15570581,-0.9355315,0.36537173,0.35791233,0.66860116,-0.72008455,0.40579385,-0.28105524,0.7084642,-0.636168,0.09691178,-0.12892953,-0.10975998,-0.479987,0.07460535,-0.4593215,-0.75755745,0.3416789,-1.1082412,0.30758795,0.5421704,0.7918487,-0.13040172,-0.6783996,-0.24897484,-0.38802254,0.4696144,-0.74002755,0.12407162,0.76970845,0.2960415,-0.30674544,-1.0314825,-0.18309677,-0.18537557,-0.48543778,0.04905686,0.16943918,0.1949126,0.2930757,0.33926663,-0.22070146,-0.32806793,-0.981253,-0.30692977,0.6269913,-0.00016888556,0.041356213,